qa_pairs.explanation:
1. Extract the proportion of the age group of 60 - 64 years old in the national population, which is 4.98%, from the 'Age distribution and proportion of the population aged 50 and above';
2. Extract the proportion of the population aged 60 and above in the national population, which is 19.8%, from the 'Population aged 60 and above and its proportion of the total population';
3. Calculate: 4.98% ÷ 19.8% = 0.2515 = 25.15%.

1. Extract the population aged 60 and above in 2023 (29697 ten thousand people) and in 2022 (28004 ten thousand people) from the 'Population aged 60 and above and its proportion of the total population', and the difference is 1693 ten thousand people;
2. Extract the total percentage of those who self - rated as 'Very well - off' (3.5%) from the 'Self - rated economic status of elderly people in urban and rural areas';
3. Calculate: 1693 × 3.5% = 59.255 = 59.26 ten thousand people.

1. Extract the population aged 60 and above in 2021 (26736 ten thousand people) from the 'Population aged 60 and above and its proportion of the total population';
2. Extract the total percentage of those who self - rated as 'Very difficult' (2.7%) from the 'Self - rated economic status of elderly people in urban and rural areas';
3. Calculate: 26736 × 2.7% = 721.872 = 721.87 ten thousand people.
